<title>POLAND: BUDIMEX TAKES SWARZEDZ TO COURT.</title>
<headline>BUDIMEX TAKES SWARZEDZ TO COURT.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction company Budimex SA took the ailing furniture maker Swarzedz SA to court to regain funds invested in Swarzedz's one-million-zloty commercial papers, Budimex said in a statement.</p>
<p>It did not give any other details and Swarzedz officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Swarzedz made a net loss of 33.9 million zlotys over this year's 10 months.</p>
<p>The company's main credtors are the Polish Development Bank (PBR) , Bank Gdanski and Powszechny Bank Gospodarczy SA (PBG). -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
